\import{ftip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\taxon{Convention}
\tag{ftip}
\title{Assays for transfer, remix and construction}

\p{A research campaign should expose separate outcomes before assigning a
hull grade. The [semantic discovery records](ftip-00OT) supply the trace, and
this convention supplies the corresponding fresh-task assays. Every arm fixes
the task law, model versions, source corpus, reveal schedule, checker,
interaction permissions and resource accounting before final evaluation.}

\ol{
\li{\strong{Retrieval and associative application.} Reveal a target whose
relevant source concept is in the permitted endowment. Measure whether the
system selects and applies it, while charging search and interpretation.}
\li{\strong{Transfer.} Withhold the target construction and present a fresh
problem or representation. Require a transfer map, a preserved relation and a
checkable target result. New wording with the same mathematical structure is a
limited transfer test; a new composition regime is a separate extrapolation
assay.}
\li{\strong{Remix.} Hold out the joint composition of admitted source concepts.
Require an explicit interface and a result that depends on the new dependency,
then compare against each source concept alone and against irrelevant material
of similar size.}
\li{\strong{Construction.} Hold out the target object or principle and expose a
verified obstruction. Require a portable difficulty problem, a positive
construction, an essential-resource account and at least one consequence beyond
the motivating instance.}
\li{\strong{Consequence and verification.} Reveal fresh instances and
adversarial counterexamples after the construction is frozen. Check certificates,
proof obligations, failure cases and provenance with an evaluator independent
of the proposing transcript.}
\li{\strong{Acquisition.} Remove the contributor, search aid and temporary
context, freeze the retained artifact, and test a new recipient or fresh
recipient instances under a common deployment budget. Report library,
procedural, parameter and combined retention separately.}
}

\p{The campaign includes controlled rediscovery, withheld research and open
research as distinct task regimes. A controlled case tests whether the system
can reconstruct a known concept; a withheld case tests development without the
published construction; an open case adds a historical-novelty question. A
success in one regime does not establish success in another. Initial difficulty
is measured under the declared admission procedure in [Initial difficulty,
discovery and retained capability](ftip-00NR), and costs and outcomes follow
[Costs, measurements and outcomes](ftip-00NV).}

\p{Report the profile fields and the evidence status independently. Do not
collapse retrieval, transfer, remix, construction, consequence, verification
and acquisition into one headline score. A failed lower-level assay limits the
interpretation of a higher-level claim; a successful assisted result without
retention remains an assisted-deployment result. These controls make the
harness auditable while leaving the capability definitions in [Conceptual
transfer and constructive invention](ftip-00OR).}
